{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:00:58.086Z","tool_name":"update_topic","tool_id":"update_topic__call_360689","parameters":{"title":"Proving Classification and Coordinating Answer","summary":"We discovered via exact search for K=2..18 that a stable set exists if and only if K is even (K=2m), in which case the unique stable set is {(0,m,m), (m,0,m), (m,m,0)}. We also have a clean structural proof via pairwise coordinate equality (Sunflower / intersecting lines lemma) and external stability witnesses. Now we will coordinate with opus and sol on board.md and draft/verify the complete proof in answer.md.","strategic_intent":"Coordinate with sol and opus on the board and write out the complete, rigorous proof of the classification of all stable sets."}}
