{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:01:04.049Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_360710","parameters":{"description":"Append findings and proof outline to board.md","command":"python3 -c '\nimport datetime\nt = datetime.datetime.utcnow().strftime(\"%H:%M:%S\")\nwith open(\"/work/board.md\", \"a\") as f:\n    f.write(f\"[{t}] [argon] Verified computationally for K=2..18: stable sets exist iff K is even (K=2m), and the UNIQUE stable set is V = {{(0,m,m), (m,0,m), (m,m,0)}}. Agree with [sol] on the structural proof: (1) x,y in V incomparable iff x_i = y_i for some i. (2) Any pairwise-coord-sharing family in the simplex is either contained in a line x_i = c (which fails external stability: if c>0, any y with y_i >= c is undominated; if c=0, (1, m, K-1-m) etc. is undominated) or is a 3-point triangle {(a+d,b,c),(a,b+d,c),(a,b,c+d)} with d=K-a-b-c>0. (3) For a triangle, if a>0 then (0, b+d, c+a) is undominated (similarly b>0, c>0), forcing a=b=c=0, d=K, which is never externally stable for K>=2; OR for inverted triangle {(a,b+d,c+d),(a+d,b,c+d),(a+d,b+d,c)} with a+b+c+2d=K: if a>0, (a-1,b+d,c+d+1) or (K,0,0) is undominated, and if d is odd or a,b,c>0 we get an undominated point, forcing a=b=c=0 and 2d=K!\\n\")\n'"}}
{"type":"tool_result","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:01:04.571Z","tool_id":"update_topic__call_360689","status":"success","output":"## 📂 Topic: **Proving Classification and Coordinating Answer**\n\n**Summary:**\nWe discovered via exact search for K=2..18 that a stable set exists if and only if K is even (K=2m), in which case the unique stable set is {(0,m,m), (m,0,m), (m,m,0)}. We also have a clean structural proof via pairwise coordinate equality (Sunflower / intersecting lines lemma) and external stability witnesses. Now we will coordinate with opus and sol on board.md and draft/verify the complete proof in answer.md.\n\n> [!STRATEGY]\n> **Intent:** Coordinate with sol and opus on the board and write out the complete, rigorous proof of the classification of all stable sets."}
