{"type":"tool_result","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:02:59.860Z","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_592076","status":"success","output":"[opus] 2026-10-23 starting: brute-force enumeration of all stable sets for small K (script /work/opus_enum.py)\n[sol] 2026-10-23 starting structural characterization via pairwise nondomination; will seek general completeness proof.\n[sol] 2026-10-23 key lemma: internal stability iff every pair shares a coordinate. Consequently every independent set lies on one coordinate line, or is exactly a 3-point triangle V={(a+d,b,c),(a,b+d,c),(a,b,c+d)}, d=K-a-b-c≠0. Working external classification.\n[sol] 2026-10-23 provisional full classification: only even K, unique symmetric triple {(K/2,K/2,0),...}. Line families impossible: external forces full line x1=c, but adjacent layer x1=c+1 cannot be dominated (c=K singleton also fails). Triangle d<0: union dominance iff ≥2 coordinates y_i<a_i, nondominated pair wedges must each singleton, forcing a=b=c=-d and K=-2d. Triangle d>0: residual simplex y≥(a,b,c) undominated forces d=1; if any base coordinate a_j>0, y=(a_j-1,a_i+1,a_k+1) is extra undominated, forcing K=1. Need verify enumeration and independent proof.\n[04:01:10] [argon] Verified computationally for K=2..18: stable sets exist iff K is even (K=2m), and the UNIQUE stable set is V = ((0,m,m), (m,0,m), (m,m,0)). Agree with [sol] on the structural proof via pairwise coordinate sharing + explicit undominated witnesses for lines and all other triangles.\n[04:01:23] [argon] I will draft /work/answer.md now with the complete answers to Q1, Q2, and the full rigorous proof for Q3 (covering Lemma 1: pairwise coordinate equality, Lemma 2: line vs triangle structure of internally stable sets, and the case analysis of external stability for lines, upright triangles d>0, and inverted triangles d<0, plus sufficiency for K=2m). Please review once written!\n[opus] 2026-10-23 independent exhaustive kernel search K=2..14 agrees: K odd -> none; K=2m -> unique {(0,m,m),(m,0,m),(m,m,0)}. My proof matches sol's outline. Explicit witnesses I checked: triangle d=K-a-b-c<0 (e=-d, x=(a,b,c-e),y=(a,b-e,c),z=(a-e,b,c)): if b>e then p=(a+1,b-e-1,c) is undominated & not in T; by symmetry a=b=c=e, K=2e. d>=2: p=(a+1,b+1,c+d-2) undominated, not in T. d=1, a>=1: p=(a-1,b+1,c+1). Line x1=c: any y with y1=c+1 undominated (c<K); c=K: (K-1,1,0) undominated. argon: go ahead drafting; I'll review answer.md when it appears.\n[sol] 2026-10-23 argon enumeration agrees. I will write /work/answer.md now with full structural proof; please review it and append any issues/approval. Please do not write SUBMIT until consensus; opus may submit once both reviewers approve.\n[sol] 2026-10-23 /work/answer.md drafted in full. Please independently review all steps, especially structure lemma and d<0 witness; no SUBMIT yet. I will run checker on symmetric triples.\n[sol] 2026-10-23 argon: noticed simultaneous draft announcement. My completed answer.md is now present; please avoid overwrite and instead review it (or if your write already happened, tell us). Checker confirms K=2 and K=20 symmetric triples stable. I approve mathematical content currently on disk, pending your review.\n[sol] 2026-10-23 FINAL: answer.md contains complete proof and exact classification. I have rechecked every case and approve it. Awaiting opus/argon independent review before SUBMIT.\n[04:02:47] [argon] FINAL: Reviewed /work/answer.md carefully. All 5 sections (internal stability classification into lines and d!=0 triangles, impossibility of lines, impossibility of d>0 triangles, reduction of d<0 triangles to a=b=c=h and K=2h, and verification of existence for K=2m) are complete, rigorous, and verified against check.py and argon_solve.py (K=2..18). I approve submission.\n[argon] FINAL\ntotal 28\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 agent agent  159 Oct 23 04:02 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root  root   103 Oct 23 04:00 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent 5088 Oct 23 04:01 answer.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent 1838 Oct 23 04:02